        "description": "<figure>\n\n<img alt=\"Isar Aerospace launching Spectrum.\" data-caption=\"\" data-portal-copyright=\"Image: Isar Aerospace\" data-has-syndication-rights=\"1\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/c-Isar-Aerospace-Flight-2_2026-09-05-224332_ylbv.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\" />\n\t<figcaption>\n\t\t</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">German company Isar Aerospace has successfully launched Europe's <a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/space/2026/09/german-company-becomes-first-in-europe-to-launch-fully-commercial-orbital-rocket/\">first entirely commercial orbital rocket</a>. It attempted to achieve the feat last March, but that lasted all of 30 seconds before the vehicle crashed into the sea and <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/news/639386/isar-aerospace-test-flight-failure-explosion\">exploded</a>. This time the company managed to get the two-stage Spectrum into low Earth orbit from a Norwegian spaceport.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-pa",
